=== HINT 1: Open handle to current thread ===
HANDLE hThread = OpenThread(THREAD_SET_CONTEXT, FALSE, GetCurrentThreadId());

=== HINT 2: Queue the APC ===
DWORD queued = QueueUserAPC((PAPCFUNC)apc_callback, hThread, 0);
// Returns non-zero on success

=== HINT 3: Alertable wait to drain the queue ===
DWORD r = SleepEx(100, TRUE);
// WAIT_IO_COMPLETION (0xC0) means one or more APCs were delivered

=== HINT 4: Assert flag ===
assert(g_apc_fired == 1);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
APC callbacks only fire when the thread is in an ALERTABLE wait:
  SleepEx(ms, TRUE), WaitForSingleObjectEx(h, ms, TRUE),
  WaitForMultipleObjectsEx(..., TRUE), etc.
For remote injection into another process:
  1. Find a thread in an alertable state (threads blocked on WaitForSingleObjectEx)
  2. OpenThread(THREAD_SET_CONTEXT, FALSE, tid)
  3. VirtualAllocEx + WriteProcessMemory for shellcode
  4. QueueUserAPC((PAPCFUNC)shellcode_addr, hThread, 0)
Early-bird APC: create process suspended, queue APC to main thread BEFORE
  ResumeThread - the APC fires before any user code runs.
